# Upstream snapshots

- Server: `standardnotes/server@65b9d74079369b3a2dbd85b42ef4e92b5e03deb4`
- App: `standardnotes/app@cb697984f4448366737f96fca0a1d3eceb941d2b`

Both trees were imported without their upstream Git history into this combined
repository. Their original license and attribution files remain in place.

## License note

`app/` is AGPL-3.0 (`app/LICENSE`, all packages declare `AGPL-3.0`).
`server/` carries an upstream inconsistency that predates this fork and was
left untouched: the `server/LICENSE` file names GPLv3, while all 19 server
packages declare `AGPL-3.0-or-later` in their `package.json` metadata. This
distribution complies with the stricter (AGPL) terms throughout — full
corresponding source is published and network deployments must offer it to
users — which satisfies either reading. See `README.md` ("Licensing").
